      "message": "We do detect literal zeros and convert them to push_zeros, but currently that happens at a later point in time:\n\nhttps://osscs.corp.google.com/skia/skia/+/main:src/sksl/codegen/SkSLRasterPipelineBuilder.cpp;l\u003d1010-1013;drc\u003db1919e9cef89f86188fb58073b71f752aabe51d2\n\nI think you\u0027re right that it makes more sense to do this conversion earlier, at `push_literal` time instead of during `makeStages`, so I wrote a followup CL that changes this behavior. That actually improves codegen a tiny bit (by allowing some adjacent zero_slots to be coalesced) but I think it\u0027s a wash for code complexity overall. \n\nI\u0027ll upload the CL once the tree unwedges a bit; it\u0027s unwieldy to constantly rebase and reupload CL chains.",
